PETsARD LLM synthesizer (petsard/synthesizer/LLM_synth)
=======================================================

This directory contains software adapted from Aug-PE.

  Project   Aug-PE: "Differentially Private Synthetic Data via Foundation
            Model APIs 2: Text" (Chulin Xie et al., ICML 2024)
  Source    https://github.com/AI-secure/aug-pe
  Revision  commit a3f292f6fec7427b6a6e6d982b83b68c1f0a86d5 (main branch,
            last commit 2025-01-11), the revision against which the files
            below were compared on 2026-10-21
  License   Apache License, Version 2.0 (full text in
            LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.txt in this directory)

Aug-PE builds on the Private Evolution implementation of microsoft/DPSDA
(https://github.com/microsoft/DPSDA, MIT License, Copyright (c) Microsoft
Corporation), as acknowledged in the Aug-PE repository.

Files adapted from Aug-PE and modified in 2026
----------------------------------------------

  synthetic_data/dpsda/dp_counter.py    from dpsda/dp_counter.py
      CPU faiss index for Windows compatibility, float32 inputs to faiss,
      comments describing the direction of the nearest-neighbour vote.

  synthetic_data/dpsda/logging.py       from dpsda/logging.py
      UTF-8 console and file logging, sample ids in the prompt log, CSV
      sample logging with header handling and a quoting fallback, the
      Checkpoint class for resumable runs; optional wandb logging removed.

  synthetic_data/feature_extractor.py   from dpsda/feature_extractor.py
      reuse of an already loaded SentenceTransformer model, checks for
      empty input and empty batches, the model returned to the caller.

  synthetic_data/main.py                Private Evolution steps (main.py)
      rewritten and extended as the SyntheticDataGenerator class used by
      the PETsARD synthesizer interface (LLM API adapters, agents,
      checkpoints and multithreaded generation).

Each of these files carries a header that names its Aug-PE origin and the
2026 modification.

Reimplemented file
------------------

  synthetic_data/dpsda/metrics.py
      Original implementation written in 2026 from the published
      definitions of the Frechet distance (FID; Heusel et al., NeurIPS 2017)
      and of k-NN precision and recall (Kynkaanniemi et al., NeurIPS 2019).
      It keeps the function names and signatures of Aug-PE dpsda/metrics.py
      (calculate_fid, knn_precision_recall_features) so that the calling
      code is unchanged, and is distributed under the MIT License of
      PETsARD (LICENSE at the repository root).

